// gzip/xz the 3 MB trajectory: below 1230 KB tightens it, ∄ kernel change.
// One command. It rescues line C or kills it honestly.

// debt(H-SEM-MEASURE, class=experiment, owner=rmw3, gate=method_unknown)
// VC-1(i) claims VSL is an optimal SOURCE CODE.
// H_tok(VSL) < H_tok(NL) is evidence ▪ ¬closure without H_sem.
// ∄ known method — Q3 asks how it would be measured at all.
// Declared so the claim is ¬quietly upgraded from open to shown.

open = {
  Q1: "is VC-1 FORMALIZABLE, or a pretty analogy? Rate-distortion needs a
       distortion function d(x, x̂); the Ω-margin is the natural candidate, but
       R(D) for a viability process is ¬trivial",
  Q2: "line D is the weakest — it needs real measured watts. Worth it, or a
       distraction?",
  Q3: "is VSL-as-optimal-source-code defensible? H_tok(VSL) < H_tok(NL) is
       evidence; the complete argument needs H_sem. How is semantic entropy
       measured at all?",
  Q4: "if this holds, is the main paper about COMPRESSION rather than
       viability — or are the two the same thing?",
  Q5: "line E is speculative and powerful. Is there literature joining
       dynamical systems + RG + information theory to cite?",
}
// Q1-Q5 were addressed TO Claude (Opus) by rmw3 on 2026-07-05 and remain
// open — kept as questions because none has been closed with evidence, and
// a question answered in a session but ¬in a document is ¬answered.

